# Vanilla-derived assets are deliberately untracked.
#
# The snow textures and their frozen byte recipes are derivatives of the user's
# installed Project Zomboid art, pending release-rights review. Committing them
# would put them in any bundle built from this repository, including reviews and
# CI that run off-machine, which the project guardrails forbid.
#
# They are fully reproducible on any machine that owns the game:
#   powershell -File tools/generate_snow_textures.ps1 -FreezeRecipe -WriteManifest
#
# assets/snow_texture_manifest.json IS tracked: it records the expected hashes and
# measurements, so a regenerated texture can still be verified byte-for-byte.
#
# NOTE: the first pattern below read `42/media/...` until 2026-07-30. A pattern
# containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so it looked for
# `<root>/42/...` and never matched the real path `mod/42/...`. The textures were
# tracked and committed for the whole life of the repository as a result. The
# pattern is fixed here; removing them from the index is a separate decision,
# because they are already in history.
mod/42/media/textures/weapons/firearm/EW_*.png
tools/recipes/*.png.seed

# In-game screenshots. Evidence for the maintainer, not source, and not ours to
# redistribute.
docs/evidence/*.png

# Build output: written by tools/validate.js on every run and read by nothing.
# It is part of the delivered tree but derived from it, so tracking it only means
# every sync dirties the working tree for no information.
artifact_manifest.json

# Assistant tooling residue. `gentle-ai skill-registry refresh` drops this into
# the project root; it describes the maintainer's local skill setup, not the mod.
# It also landed inside the installed PZ mod folder once, which broke the
# output/install parity audit in tools/sync_development_build.ps1.
.atl/
